  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Max gets a ride home after a long and exhausting day. He talks about the massive amount of cooking he had to do. Let's listen closely to their exchange in Russian first, and then walk through each line together.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Садись, я тебя подкину до дома.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, я очень устал сегодня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ну что, как твои дела?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нормально, всё хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ты приготовил новые блюда?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, приготовил двенадцать всяких блюд.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Звучит очень вкусно и интересно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я очень старался на кухне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Тебе нравится твоя новая работа?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мне всё очень нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ты быстро учишься, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, я буду стараться дальше.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Садись, я тебя подкину до дома.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Get in, I will give you a lift home.' Listen for the word meaning 'sit down' right alongside 'I' in this line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, я очень устал сегодня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you, I am very tired today.' Notice the word order: 'thank you' comes first, and 'today' finishes the sentence. Vika answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ну что, как твои дела?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well then, how are your affairs?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'what' straight to 'things'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нормально, всё хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Normally, everything is fine.' You'll hear 'fine' all the time in the show, here connected with 'good'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ты приготовил новые блюда?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you prepare new dishes?' The first content word means 'you', and 'of dish' rounds out the thought. Then Max replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, приготовил двенадцать всяких блюд.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I prepared twelve kinds of dishes.' Max starts with 'cooked' and pairs it with 'twelve' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Звучит очень вкусно и интересно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Sounds very tasty and interesting.' Vika starts with 'sounds' and pairs it with 'very much' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я очень старался на кухне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I tried very hard in the kitchen.' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'kitchen' in a very natural everyday phrasing. And Vika jumps in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Тебе нравится твоя новая работа?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you like your new job?' Here 'for you' sets up the idea, while 'job' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, мне всё очень нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, I like everything very much.' A compact expression built around 'to me' and 'is pleasing'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anja",
      "t": "Ты быстро учишься, молодец.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You learn quickly, well done.' Vika starts with 'you' and pairs it with 'quickly' to make the point clear. Max answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо, я буду стараться дальше.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you, I will try further.' The reflexive ending on the verb for 'to try' turns the action back onto the subject. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
